{"version":1,"ops":[{"type":3,"author":{"id":"bfb0c87a087f143d5d4fb3c3b303347e581f98d0"},"timestamp":1511217415,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDM0NTg1NDg5Ng==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/1974#issuecomment-345854896"},"message":"unfortunately that is how things are, see e.g. https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/1798 for the related discussion.  Also it relates I guess to the another discussion of ambiguity in the API here -- are you trying to just add a subdataset, or all the files under it and now we do both kinda (thus that file gets committed)\nWay of things/workarounds: either\n- use `--to-git` when you `datalad add` for a particular file, or just `datalad save` before you do `add -d . submodule`\n- (preferred) define that all or some specific files in that repo should go under git (`.gitattributes` file rules).  E.g. you could have used `datalad create --text-no-annex` when creating the repo to prepropulate that rule so any text file (but not an empty file) would be committed to git since then we would add \n```\n* annex.largefiles=(not(mimetype=text/*))\n```\nto that repo `.gitattributes`.  May be @mih or @bpoldrack could provide a better advice","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1540753028,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDQzMzczMTcyNA==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/1974#issuecomment-433731724"},"message":"Here is what happens with https://github.com/datalad/datalad-revolution. Bottom line: same switch to annex without a dedicated flag, but ability to target a dataset as a whole, instead of all its content (unless explicitly indicated via rsync-like syntax or `--recursive`):\n\n```\n(datalad3-dev) mih@meiner /tmp % datalad rev-create test_dataset\n[INFO   ] Creating a new annex repo at /tmp/test_dataset \ncreate(ok): /tmp/test_dataset (dataset)\n(datalad3-dev) mih@meiner /tmp % cd test_dataset\n(datalad3-dev) mih@meiner /tmp/test_dataset (git)-[master] % datalad rev-create subdataset\n[INFO   ] Creating a new annex repo at /tmp/test_dataset/subdataset \ncreate(ok): /tmp/test_dataset/subdataset (dataset)\n(datalad3-dev) mih@meiner /tmp/test_dataset (git)-[master] % datalad rev-save\nsave(ok): .\n(datalad3-dev) mih@meiner /tmp/test_dataset (git)-[master] % git st\nOn branch master\nnothing to commit, working tree clean\n(datalad3-dev) mih@meiner /tmp/test_dataset (git)-[master] % tig\n(datalad3-dev) mih@meiner /tmp/test_dataset (git)-[master] % cd subdataset\n(datalad3-dev) mih@meiner /tmp/test_dataset/subdataset (git)-[master] % touch myfileingit.txt\n(datalad3-dev) mih@meiner /tmp/test_dataset/subdataset (git)-[master] % git add myfileingit.txt\n(datalad3-dev) mih@meiner /tmp/test_dataset/subdataset (git)-[master] % git commit -m \"Added file\"\n[master a0822e7] Added file\n 1 file changed, 0 insertions(+), 0 deletions(-)\n create mode 100644 myfileingit.txt\n(datalad3-dev) mih@meiner /tmp/test_dataset/subdataset (git)-[master] % cd ..\n(datalad3-dev) mih@meiner /tmp/test_dataset (git)-[master] % git st\nOn branch master\nChanges not staged for commit:\n  (use \"git add \u003cfile\u003e...\" to update what will be committed)\n  (use \"git checkout -- \u003cfile\u003e...\" to discard changes in working directory)\n\n        modified:   subdataset (new commits)\n\nno changes added to commit (use \"git add\" and/or \"git commit -a\")\n(datalad3-dev) mih@meiner /tmp/test_dataset (git)-[master] % datalad rev-save\nsave(ok): .\n(datalad3-dev) mih@meiner /tmp/test_dataset (git)-[master] % ls -l subdataset/myfileingit.txt\n-rw-rw-r-- 1 mih mih 0 Oct 28 19:51 subdataset/myfileingit.txt\n(datalad3-dev) mih@meiner /tmp/test_dataset (git)-[master] % echo \"adding stuff\" \u003e\u003e subdataset/myfileingit.txt\n(datalad3-dev) mih@meiner /tmp/test_dataset (git)-[master] % datalad rev-save\n\n# nothing happened (no committed changes in subdataset)\n\n(datalad3-dev) mih@meiner /tmp/test_dataset (git)-[master] % ls -l subdataset\ntotal 4\n-rw-rw-r-- 1 mih mih 13 Oct 28 19:53 myfileingit.txt\n(datalad3-dev) mih@meiner /tmp/test_dataset (git)-[master] % datalad rev-save --recursive\nadd(ok): myfileingit.txt (file)\nsave(ok): subdataset\nsave(ok): .\naction summary:\n  add (ok: 1)\n  save (ok: 2)\n(datalad3-dev) mih@meiner /tmp/test_dataset (git)-[master] % ls -l subdataset\ntotal 4\nlrwxrwxrwx 1 mih mih 118 Oct 28 19:53 myfileingit.txt -\u003e .git/annex/objects/x4/xK/MD5E-s13--ef8174b2381e2ac9c2b0f2a8a39e5031.txt/MD5E-s13--ef8174b2381e2ac9c2b0f2a8a39e5031.txt\n```","files":null}]}